AB  - EEG signal feature extracting and classification are hot topics in cerebral nerve information processing and have attracted great attention nowadays with the emergence of Large-scale data. Aiming at problem of the insufficient accuracy of automatic sleep staging and process continuous data, a new method of automatic sleep staging based on a fusion algorithm, multi-scale entropy (MSE) and principal component analysis (PCA), is proposed. In this work, the data of sleep EEG monitoring and the expert staging of eight groups are utilized as samples. Firstly, MSE is used to extract the nonlinear dynamic features from sleep stages. Then these features are replaced by the first two principal component vectors of PCA. The purpose is to reduce the data dimension redundancy, as well as retaining the majority of EEG non-linear features. After that, the new vectors are entered into the BPNN classifier to implement the MSE-PCA model of automatic sleep staging. The experimental results from MIT-BIH physiological information database show that this MSE-PCA features extracting method is suitable for large-scale and real-time data processing and the accuracy of automatic staging can reach 87.9%, which can improve the accuracy and stability of automatic EEG sleep staging system.
