AB  - Neural mass model has been widely used to fit electroencephalographic signal and track brain states. In this study, unscented Kalman filter was applied to estimate parameters of Jansen-Rit (JR) neural mass model and track the real electroencephalogram (EEG) recordings. The power spectral and the Permutation Entropy (PeEn) demonstrated its good performance in tracking EEG signals from the perspectives of frequency domain and complexity respectively. The parameter estimates indicated that propofol caused a decrease in the rate constant of inhibitory post-synaptic potential (p < 0.001, repeated measures ANOVA) as is generally observed in physiology. Moreover, it was found that there were significant differences between awake state and anesthetized state in estimated parameters. The results suggest that the combination of neural mass model and unscented Kalman filter is a powerful tool for inferring underlying physiological information of brain state.
