AB  - As a necessary process of life, sleep is an important part of the body rehabilitation, integration and consolidating memories, is an integral part of health. Recently, a lot of people are suffering from sleep diseases, such as insomnia, which aroused the interest of a large number of scholars to research on sleep, and this has a certain realistic guiding significance. By using nonlinear dynamics theory knowledge, The Jenson-Shannon Divergence(JSD) algorithm and the multiscale JSD algorithm are proposed to research on the alpha EEG signals and theta EEG signals which in conscious period and Non-rapid Eye Movement(NREM) sleep stage I in this paper. At the same time, we also use the SPSS statistical software to verify the results of two experiments about the EEG in alpha band and theta band in two different states, the results of two groups got a very good effect both in the accuracy and reliability. In addition, we analyzed the alpha EEG in two states with the method of error bar graph, the research results show that both the JSD algorithm and the improved multi-scale JSD algorithm can effectively distinguish the EEG signals both in awaked period and NREM sleep stage I, which is unified with the scientific basis, namely the alpha waves in eeg signals are more than the other waves when people are awaked, however, there are more theta waves in eeg signals when people are in state of NREM sleep stage I (shallow sleep phases), proved that the EEG signals in two states exist significant differences, which also tell me that the algorithm we proposed can be further used in the study of sleep EEG in installment, which can be provided to help all kinds of disease diagnosis and treatment of sleep with effective auxiliary function, the research has an important practical significance.
