AB  - In communication theory, information measures answer two fundamental questions, viz: the ultimate data compression (by entropy) and the ultimate transmission rate (by the channel capacity). In case of brain and the study of brain function analyzing EEG, the information measures help to show how entropy can be used to remove redundancy in EEG and consequently making it useful for monitoring of brain function in critical conditions and secondly on how information transmission measures describe normal e.g. sleep stages and divergence from normal e.g epilepsy or ischemic brain injury.
