AB  - This article first introduces a data acquisition and analysis system for consciousness state information based on signal sensors, and compares the brain electrical signals of patients with micro-consciousness with normal and vegetative states. This study analyzed the neural oscillations and energy distribution of patients in the micro-conscious state, and found that the EEG amplitude of the micro-conscious state patients was greater than that of the vegetative state but less than the normal state, and the delta frequency band density in the signal was high but the high-frequency energy was lacking. This paper introduces 6 entropy algorithms and proposes a simpler and faster minimum Renyi sorting entropy based on Renyi sorting entropy.
