AB  - As a chronic progressive and neurodegenerative disorder to threaten elders worldwide, dementia always gradually develops from mild forgetfulness to severe cognitive decline and covers several clinical conditions including Alzheimer's disease (AD) and Mild cognition impairment (MCI). Timely and precise diagnosis of patients with different dementia diseases are essential for effectively medical intervention. Virtual reality (VR) has been proved to activate functional connectivity among multiple cortical regions to varying degrees for humans with different cognitive levels, presenting good potential to take part in neuropsychological test especially for dementia. Electroencephalography (EEG) is commonly used to clinically evaluate the brain activity of neurological diseases such as epilepsy, sleep disorders, and brain tumors, with good time resolution. Graph theory can robustly represent the topological properties of intricate brain functional connectivity based on EEG data. Accordingly, we convene AD patients, MCI patients, and healthy controls, to watch VR 3D videos and simultaneously measure their EEG data to constitute the functional networks. The p-values statistically demonstrated a neural differentiation of the functional small-world network among AD, MCI, and normal controls under 3D cognitive loads. The significantly different functional connectivities between three dementia groups indicate that the 3D simulation expertise can be applied in clinical dementia diagnosis.
