AB  - Automatic sleep stage classification is an important area of research for various clinical applications. Using Electrooculogram (EOG) signal for sleep stage scoring may provide inexpensive, easy to use solution with further possibility for mobile monitoring of sleep and health in general. In this paper, a single channel EOG based sleep stage classificaition method is presented. Various moment based and entropy based features are extracted from Discrete Wavelet Transform (DWT) bands of the EOG signals. A resampling methodology is used based on Synthetic Minority Oversampling Technique (SMOTE) to balance the training data. An Extreme Gradient Boosting (XGBoost) classifier is used for classification. The performance of the classifier is studied using a subject independent validation scheme on a publicly available database. The results show that the proposed method overcomes some limitations of the existing literature such as class imbalance, poor detection accuracy of $N_{1}$ sleep stage and subject to subject variations. The proposed method outperforms various EEG and EOG based methods in the existing literature in terms of detection accuracy of $N_{1}$ sleep stage. Moreover, a state-of-the-art EOG based method is implemented with subject independent evaluation and compared with the proposed method. The results show that, the proposed method performs better in terms of precision, recall, f1-score and accuracy.
