AB  - In human life, one of the crucial roles is played by emotions. Emotions are nothing but expressions of human psychology and physiology and they are related to the physical and mental states of the human being. Due to the rising advent of the brain computer interface (BCI) compiled with Pattern Recognition (PR) techniques, emotion classification from electroencephalography (EEG) has attracted a lot of attention. In this work, an interesting model is proposed for the analysis of emotion classification and recognition from EEG signals. The strategy utilizes the concept of Empirical Mode Decomposition (EMD), Variational Mode Decomposition (VMD), Sample Entropy, Ant Lion Optimization (ALO) with Extreme Learning Machine (ELM) known altogether as EVSAE model. The work is evaluated on two publicly available datasets, such as DREAMER and DEAP, and the best results are analyzed for both the datasets comprehensively.
