AB  - Sleepiness is a main causal factor for accidents and daytime malfunction. In this study we checked the feasibility of a new, ECG based method to detect the propensity to fall asleep while driving, using a passive Maintenance of Wakefulness Test (MWT) and an active Driving Simulation (DS) during increasing sleep deprivation conditions. Microsleeps (MS), and falling asleep (FA) events, were detected from electroencephalogram analysis. HRV was characterized using Time Domain analysis, Time Frequency Decomposition, Entropy, and Poincaré plots.
