AB  - This study proposes a novel hybrid deep learning model, DeepEEG, which effectively addresses the challenge of relaxation state recognition posed by EEG signal complexity and individual variability through the integration of CNN, BiLSTM, and multi-head self-attention mechanisms. The model utilizes CNN to extract spatial features, BiLSTM to capture temporal dynamics, and the multi-head self-attention mechanism to focus on key time frames. Experimental results on the DEAP dataset demonstrate a classification accuracy of 95.8%, significantly outperforming baseline models such as SVM, CNN, and BiLSTM. Ablation experiments validate the effectiveness of each component, particularly the multi-head attention mechanism. This model provides a robust solution for EEG-based psychological state decoding and holds application potential in mental health monitoring.
