AB  - A Seizure is a sudden, uncontrollable electrical disturbance in the brain that can cause changes in behaviour, movements, sensation or consciousness. It can be caused by various factors such as epilepsy, head injuries, infections or medication side effects. Seizure detection using machine learning involves developing algorithms that can accurately detect seizures in electroencephalogram (EEG) recordings. This is a challenging task due to the complex and variable nature of seizures, as well as the presence of various artifacts in EEG signals. Machine learning approaches have shown promise in addressing these challenges by leveraging features extracted from EEG signals to classify seizure and non-seizure states. In this approach, the raw dataset will go through a Discrete Wavelet Transform to further sample down the dataset to increase the accuracy of the results acquired by feature extraction. Then, Support Vector Machine Algorithm is used to find the efficiency of the modified dataset as it has one of the highest accuracy with respect to other machine learning algorithms. At last, with the help of Artificial Neural Network, a weighted neural network is formed to help in the real-world applications. Using the single board computers, the weighted neural network can be used in real-time to find out the presence of the seizure in the patients.
