AB  - Traditional feature extraction methods describe signals in terms of amplitude and frequency. This paper takes a paradigm shift and investigates four stochastic-complexity features. Their advantages are demonstrated on synthetic and physiological signals; the latter recorded during periods of Cheyne-Stokes respiration, anesthesia, sleep, and motor-cortex investigation.
