AB  - Hirayama disease is a self-limiting cervical motor neuron disease, usually affecting the spinal cord at level C7-T1. We share an unusual case of Hirayama disease in a young man affecting roots C4-C6. He presented in coma due to diaphragm weakness and hypercapnic respiratory failure. Diagnosis was achieved via clinical presentation, neurophysiological examination, ultrasonography of the diaphragm and dynamic MR-imaging. Conservative treatment with a cervical collar resulted in remarkable improvement in respiratory and motor function.
DO  - 10.1016/j.ajem.2023.11.049
