AB  - This is an adaptation of a script that was originally designed for hypnosis testing in an fMRI scanner environment. This script has been influenced by phenomenological approaches to measuring hypnotic responsiveness as well as the issue of testing experiential suggestions which may or may not be formally defined as hypnosis. This is a short procedure able to be administered in 10 minutes. It may be administered without reference to hypnosis as an absorption induction. Alternatively it may be used as a hypnotic induction preceding further specific hypnotic suggestions. The present script is suitable as either an absorption or a hypnosis induction in experimental and clinical settings, including of course scanner environments. With the inclusion of the PCI it offers a sensitive way to assess the phenomenology of changes in consciousness associated with the induction process and potentially trait absorption and trait hypnotic susceptibility. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2025 APA, all rights reserved)
