AB  - This international selection of 34 papers from the conference Toward a Science of Consciousness (Tokyo, 1999) held ant the United Nations University gives a valuable state of the art overview of consciousness research. Approaches from European, American and Japanese researchers are presented. The book provides a world-wide audience with a comprehensive outlook for the potential contribution to the future of consciousness research. Included is the Tokyo '99 declaration to promote scientists' ethical warning against the thoughtless use of consciousness research in warfare. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2026 APA, all rights reserved)
