KW  - *Human Biological Rhythms
KW  - *Measurement
KW  - *Performance
KW  - *Sleep Onset
AB  - Analyzed data from published research reports showing normal nonrandom fluctuations in daily human performance associated with worker error, vehicle crashes, and occurrence of disease-related deaths. Data were fitted with a 2-peak-per-day cosine curve derived from the population growth function used in chaos theory. Median parameters extracted from the curve fits predicted a sharp peak of sleepiness at 2:30 AM and a secondary peak at 2:30 PM. The shape of the curve was modified by a nonlinear sleep-deprivation factor. The model appears to be biological rather than behavioral or social because it applied well to disease-related deaths. Methods for the measurement of sleepiness including electroencephalographic monitoring of sleep, self-report techniques, pupillography, and the Multiple Sleep Latency and the Maintenance of Wakefulness Tests are also reviewed. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2022 APA, all rights reserved)
DO  - https://dx.doi.org/10.1080/08964289.1996.9933755
