CY  - US
T3  - PsycCRITIQUES
KW  - *Consciousness States
KW  - *Dreaming
AB  - Consciousness, its biophysiological, sociocultural, and intrapsychic aspects, is the subject of the conceptually bold volume, Consciousness, Dreams, and Self: A Transdisciplinary Approach (see record 1996-98124-000). The author is a practicing psychologist and academic with an obvious passion for wide-ranging integrative thinking. There is a nexus here of evolutionary biology, ethology, comparative neuroanatomy, primatology, mathematics, general systems theory, and the psychology of self and of dream states. The dream state is selected for special study because it is one state of consciousness shared by all humans and is clearly affected by factors that are biophysiological, sociocultural, and intrapsychic. Arden is clearly able to move comfortably through a complex subject and share with the reader his appreciation for it. I learned quite a bit from this volume and trust that readers lacking a background in science or mathematics will too. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2021 APA, all rights reserved)
DO  - https://dx.doi.org/10.1037/000233
ER  -

