AB  - [proposed] a universal mechanism of self-similar neural dynamics extending from individual neurons to the whole brain / the proposed mechanism [is based on chaos theory and] links the different scales conceptually (since they use the same dynamics) and it links them literally, via the notion of between-scales influence / in this sense the brain is doubly chaotic / 1st, neural dynamics can move into the chaotic regime at any given scale S of organization / 2nd, even in the special case where all systems S are engaged in ordered limit cycles, the recursively modular structure of the brain means that global EEG will have a fractal dimension / this is due to the wheels within wheels nature of the brain's meta-organization / this may explain why fully engaged conscious activity, utilizing the full fractal depth of the brain, is only surpassed in its fractal dimension by the EEG of schizophrenics and REM sleep this fluid, recursively organized, nonlinear dynamical system evolves at the edge of chaos, moving variously between order and chaos at the multiple scales (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2021 APA, all rights reserved)
