AB  - Explores how neuroimaging methods can augment behavioral methods to discover processing stages. Event related brain potentials, brain electrical source analysis (BESA) and regional changes in cerebral blood flow (rCBF) do not necessarily require behavioral responses. Studies on attention, simple motor, and combined visual and memory search tasks give evidence for modularity, and indicate that preprocessing and feature extraction stages can be distinguished, but the latter has several submodules differing in time and space. BESA describes cortical activity with high temporal resolution in terms of limited numbers of neural generators within brain systems in the imaging of visual, cognitive, and manual motor processors. Several cortical and subcortical brain systems active in selective attention and memory search tasks are discovered with the help of rCBF. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2021 APA, all rights reserved)
DO  - https://dx.doi.org/10.1016/0001-6918%2895%2900035-S
