KW  - *Artificial Intelligence
KW  - *Cognitive Processes
KW  - *Creativity
KW  - Computers
KW  - Unconscious (Personality Factor)
AB  - What is creativity? Can science ever explain it? "The Creative Mind" shows how the latest research in artificial intelligence sheds new light on an ancient mystery. Traditionally, we have viewed the creative individual as genius, lunatic, or, at the very least, divinely inspired. In this bold and provocative new book, Margaret Boden brilliantly dismantles these romantic conceptions. Drawing on an innovative approach called "computational" psychology, Boden outlines the thought process and mental structures in which our creativity is grounded. She examines how the unconscious devises novel associations, how we learn to form new analogies, and how we come to break out of familiar conceptual frameworks in order to produce a creative idea. With examples ranging from story writing to chess to physics, from jazz improvisation to the diagnosis of soybean disease, she explains how all forms of creativity spring from the same cognitive devices and mental maps, demonstrating how the average person's creativity is related to that of Mozart or a Shakespeare. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2021 APA, all rights reserved)
